course: dictionary
lesson: 12496
title: Dented: pushed in or hurt
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dented means pushed in a little, usually because something was hit. A dented can has a dip in its side. «The old can was dented when it fell off the shelf.» The clue is the dip, not a hole or a tear.
explain: The word also describes feelings. «His dented pride made him go quiet after he lost the match.» Pride cannot be pushed in like metal, so here dented means his pride was hurt or weakened.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The helmet was dented» means the helmet has a dip in it, so it may no longer protect your head.
fact: Dented means having a dent or dents: pushed in a little by being hit.
fact: Dented is also the past form of the verb dent: dent, dents, denting, dented.
fact: «Dented pride» means pride that has been hurt or weakened, as in «dented confidence».
fact: A dented bike helmet should be replaced, because it may no longer protect your head.
exercise: «The can was dented when it fell off the shelf.» What does dented mean? | Full to the top | Painted bright red | *Pushed in a little by being hit | Cold and wet
exercise: Dad says, «The helmet is dented, so we must get a new one.» Why? | It is too heavy | *It may no longer protect your head | Dented helmets look old | It has the wrong colour
exercise: «His dented pride made him go quiet after he lost the match.» What is dented here? | Full of water | Made of tin | *Hurt or weakened | Shiny and new
test: «The car door was dented in the car park.» What is the door like? | Clean | *Pushed in a little | Painted | Opened
test: Which sentence uses dented to show hurt feelings? | *«Her dented confidence made her stop trying.» | «The pan was dented on the stove.» | «The can was dented when it fell.» | «The box was dented on the bus.»
exam: Ben says his bike helmet is dented but still looks fine. What should he do and why? | Give it to his sister | Paint it so the dent does not show | *Get a new one, because a dented helmet may no longer protect him | Keep wearing it, because it still looks fine
